Chapter: PowOnReal

 There is no floating-point exponentiation routine in the runtime, so the
 only thing the emitter could do with a Real is hand two IEEE-754 bit
 patterns to an integer square-and-multiply, which computes nothing. That is
 the same shape as the integer comparator on Reals, which `CDX9010` exists
 to refuse, and the same shape as `unit Real` arithmetic reaching the
 integer adder.

Section: Report

  rpow : Real, Real -> Real
  rpow (a) (b) = a ^ b

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni (show (real-to-bits (rpow 2.0 3.0)))
  end
